SOAPBOX: This was another last-minute WQ6X CQ-160 contest, running the WA6TQT
SOAPBOX: Superstation in Anza, with its "crippled" 100-ft high "Tri-Square" array.
SOAPBOX: The antenna height made for a nice barefoot signal, however I could
SOAPBOX: never tell which direction favored my signal (if at all). Most of the action
SOAPBOX: happened on Friday evening. Saturday was largely a ho-hummer so most
SOAPBOX: of the OP time was spent in the Winter Field Day.
SOAPBOX: Look for a write-up on this GiG at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com.
